<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Głogów</h1><p class="st-meta">1251 CE – 1506 CE (approx.) · capital Głogów</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Silesian Piast duchy on the Oder whose dukes claimed Greater Poland, later a Bohemian fief held briefly by the future King Sigismund I of Poland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konrad-i-of-glogow">Konrad I</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-the-pious">Henry II the Pious</a>, received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glogow">Głogów</a> and the lands around it in a division of the Silesian inheritance around 1251. Głogów, a fortified town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oder-river">Oder</a>, became the capital of a duchy covering much of northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Silesia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konrad-i-of-glogow">Konrad</a>'s son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-glogow">Henry III of Głogów</a> was one of the most powerful Silesian princes, holding <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-greater-poland">Greater Poland</a> for a time and claiming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Polish crown</a>. After him the duchy was divided among branches, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagan">Żagań</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olesnica">Oleśnica</a>. Half of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glogow">Głogów</a> passed directly to the Bohemian crown in 1331, and the remaining dukes became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia</a>. German settlement and town law transformed the region.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piast</a> lines died out and disputes followed, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glogow">Głogów</a> was granted to the Jagiellonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-i-the-old">Sigismund</a>, who ruled it from 1499 until 1506 before becoming King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. It then returned to the Bohemian crown, passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1742, and to Poland in 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-glogow.jpg" alt="Duchy of Głogów" width="320" height="336"><figcaption>Image: Zuber · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silesia_1249-1273.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1251 CE – 1506 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Głogów</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Konrad I of Głogów, Henry III of Głogów, Sigismund I the Old</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polish, German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of Glogau, Duchy of Glogow</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1378&amp;focus=duchy-of-glogow" aria-label="Duchy of Głogów on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5043 390 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Głogów lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5363 646L5367 659M5363 646L5330 692M5363 646L5387 662M5363 646L5346 648M5363 646L5372 653M5363 646L5394 659"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5367 659h0M5330 692h0M5387 662h0M5346 648h0M5372 653h0M5394 659h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5363 646h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5363 646h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Głogów. <a href="/atlas?year=1378&amp;focus=duchy-of-glogow">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
